      },
      "Observability tip": {
        "frame": "deep_cyan",
        "ground": "pale_cyan"
      }
    }
  },
  "color_roles": {
    "note": "The base palette is the DOCX/document palette, where these colours are used as light fills behind dark text. The XeLaTeX guidance boxes put white title text ON these colours, which needs a darker value to reach 4.5:1 -- DOCX amber on white text is only 2.38:1. Same token, different role, so the LaTeX frame values are recorded separately rather than pretending one value serves both.",
